[[:db/retract 17592186120525 :question/answer-fields 17592186119264] {:db/id 17592186119821 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1098aac8-90b3-5ba0-b447-7ead2947d568"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1098aac8-90b3-5ba0-b447-7ead2947d568" :question/id #uuid "1098aac8-90b3-5ba0-b447-7ead2947d568" :question/math-academy-id "q-35247" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}-4(5)=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+5=9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9bd25317-6ae7-5ed2-b2f8-06a74441129a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9bd25317-6ae7-5ed2-b2f8-06a74441129a" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd25317-6ae7-5ed2-b2f8-06a74441129a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-54b2da92-80e1-5a61-a19c-e0402c5db36e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ccdbeb50-bd46-5e6a-a5d9-d2fa3f1bb293" "answer-94ec8a9d-591d-59ec-b9c5-a655500ebc04" "answer-f2716f4b-b756-5daf-b7ff-420d367fb480" "answer-54b2da92-80e1-5a61-a19c-e0402c5db36e" "answer-c791cf81-feb5-59a1-bf25-b0be74c138f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccdbeb50-bd46-5e6a-a5d9-d2fa3f1bb293" :answer/id #uuid "ccdbeb50-bd46-5e6a-a5d9-d2fa3f1bb293" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94ec8a9d-591d-59ec-b9c5-a655500ebc04" :answer/id #uuid "94ec8a9d-591d-59ec-b9c5-a655500ebc04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2716f4b-b756-5daf-b7ff-420d367fb480" :answer/id #uuid "f2716f4b-b756-5daf-b7ff-420d367fb480" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54b2da92-80e1-5a61-a19c-e0402c5db36e" :answer/id #uuid "54b2da92-80e1-5a61-a19c-e0402c5db36e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c791cf81-feb5-59a1-bf25-b0be74c138f2" :answer/id #uuid "c791cf81-feb5-59a1-bf25-b0be74c138f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120525 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=2\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-4)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c652bfa5-8e6a-53fc-ad6f-da352c6f194d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c652bfa5-8e6a-53fc-ad6f-da352c6f194d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c652bfa5-8e6a-53fc-ad6f-da352c6f194d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-460c227b-da50-5240-a61b-5d7158cbefb0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ca59db9a-208c-56e6-9d14-d390aecd3368" "answer-460c227b-da50-5240-a61b-5d7158cbefb0" "answer-b96e7099-61f5-552d-a37f-75ea4d0acd7b" "answer-c28d8b2c-0794-5b52-be1a-1a5068c24206" "answer-04f5fc79-efcf-5beb-8f44-6c5bbee2e205"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca59db9a-208c-56e6-9d14-d390aecd3368" :answer/id #uuid "ca59db9a-208c-56e6-9d14-d390aecd3368" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-460c227b-da50-5240-a61b-5d7158cbefb0" :answer/id #uuid "460c227b-da50-5240-a61b-5d7158cbefb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b96e7099-61f5-552d-a37f-75ea4d0acd7b" :answer/id #uuid "b96e7099-61f5-552d-a37f-75ea4d0acd7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value